(2) Troubleshooting
No sensor data

Error:
probe_eddy_current sensor outage

Cause:

I2C failure

MCU not responding

Check:

i2c_bus

i2c_mcu

wiring

Calibration fails monotonic check

Error:

Failed calibration - frequency not increasing each step


Cause:

Metal under bed

Probe tilted

Electrical noise

Fix:

Raise probe slightly

Remove steel sheet

Re-run calibration

Virtual contact crashes nozzle

Cause:

Wrong z_offset

Bad calibration

Fix:

Recalibrate

Increase z_offset

Lower vir_contact_speed

Mesh warped or shifted

Cause:

Wrong X/Y offsets

Fix:

Measure nozzle → probe offsets physically

(3) Offset Diagram

Top view:

      +Y
       ↑
       |
       |   Probe (eddy)
       |     ●
       |
       |        Nozzle
       |          ●
       +----------------→ +X


Offsets:

probe_x = nozzle_x + x_offset
probe_y = nozzle_y + y_offset


Your config:

x_offset = -16.43   (probe is left of nozzle)
y_offset =  10.22   (probe is in front of nozzle)

(4) Safe Macro Examples
Safe virtual contact test
[gcode_macro TEST_VIR_CONTACT]
gcode:
  G91
  G1 Z5 F300
  G90
  G1 X150 Y150 F6000
  RUN_PROBE_VIR_CONTACT

Safe Z home macro
[gcode_macro HOME_Z_EDDY]
gcode:
  G91
  G1 Z5 F300
  G90
  G1 X150 Y150 F6000
  RUN_PROBE_VIR_CONTACT
  G92 Z0

Safe mesh macro
[gcode_macro MESH_EDDY]
gcode:
  BED_MESH_CLEAR
  BED_MESH_CALIBRATE METHOD=rapid_scan
  BED_MESH_PROFILE SAVE=eddy

Summary

PROBE_EDDY_CURRENT_CALIBRATE builds height→frequency map

METHOD=scan = pause & sample

METHOD=rapid_scan = sample while moving

RUN_PROBE_VIR_CONTACT = eddy probe pretending to be contact

X/Y offsets are used explicitly during calibration

Z offset is used both as trigger reference and probe offset